{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592670-recognizing-a-werewolf-in-different-forms","id":592670,"title":"Recognizing a Werewolf in different forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T08:45:04-07:00","id":592670,"title":"Recognizing a Werewolf in different forms","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> If one Garou meets a werewolf that is in Homid Form, and later find that same werewolf in lupus, would he be able to recognize as the same werewolf (provided, of course, that he didn't saw the guy changing in neither moment)? <br /> <br /> I'm sure that someone that is not a Garou would not recognize, unless there was very distinct traits (like a tatoo or something like it). But I understand that Garou work with different senses other than just sight, so I don't know if there would be a smell or a &quot;primal-urge&quot; way to get it.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5426-aecioborba","name":"aecioborba","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T09:27:14-07:00","id":592737,"title":"","content":"By default? No.<br /> <br /> Though there are lots of starting level powers that would at least justify a roll to figure it out. It also depends on a number of factors. Battles Scars and deformities, for example, are going to carry over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:03:45-07:00","id":592856,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would assume that once werewolves spend a few years in Garou society, they roughly know how mannerisms and body language translate to different forms, just like you can identify your friends even when they wear different (heavy) clothing. Thus: A &quot;primal urge&quot; way, at least regarding people they've had time to study.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:11:53-07:00","id":592979,"title":"","content":"I usually describe the creature to my players, and when they ask if they know them and actively take a closer look, I give them the solution based mainly on smell and superficial physical similarities, without a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:50:52-07:00","id":593062,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't even ask for Primal Urge in case of a well known friend. Even completely human friends would have a good chance at recognising him if they could stand Lunacy and accept what they're seeing.<br /> <br /> That aside, you could ascribe Primal Urge to sense the smell of someone you don't know that much, but in Homid it would require at least an active and proximal action. It would be easier in Lupus form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:06:42-07:00","id":593458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592670-recognizing-a-werewolf-in-different-forms?p=592737#post592737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default? No.<br /> <br /> Though there are lots of starting level powers that would at least justify a roll to figure it out. It also depends on a number of factors. Battles Scars and deformities, for example, are going to carry over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. There's really no connection between one's homid and lupus forms. There could be some kind of connection - some players like to have some kind of markings show up in some way between forms - but not to the extent it could ever relied upon. However, changes onto the body afterwards - battle scars, missing limbs, etc. - will be reflected. One of the few ways werewolves were recognized in folktales is that damage done to the werewolf - a bullet wound, cutting off a paw - would subsequently identify the human who had turned into that wolf.<br /> <br /> However, the most likely way a werewolf could identify the other is not by sight, but by smell. I'd be more willing to allow both homid and lupus forms to have some kind of common element of scent, although I'd likely require a Primal Urge roll with minimum of three successes. Only one or two might be, &quot;there's something familiar about the scent,&quot; and leave it to the player to guess correctly. After all, the homid and lupus forms do not have the same glands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-16-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}